#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df9a543-b5df-589d-9923-b17fb9588714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{4}{3},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549338} {:answer/id #uuid "3d610a34-2b2c-5b7f-a6ee-1208ff230466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549439} {:answer/id #uuid "5d61e674-449f-5c1e-8470-6d7a912ecbd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\frac{1}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549503} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1dd293-3094-5184-81d3-8f43b189007b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549619} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f407d3-59e6-5e5d-8e6f-2e775ce3251f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{4}{3},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1dd293-3094-5184-81d3-8f43b189007b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549619} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8e4aed-0ad7-583b-bf1d-eb2a74efae0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bfd7586-e0f5-50a2-a9b8-3d8eb173ed99" :question/math-academy-id "q-35155" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{3}(x+2)(x-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-\\frac{1}{3}<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-2+2}{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=0$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x+2)(x-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(0+2)(0-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(0,\\frac{4}{3}),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\frac{4}{3}].$\n\n![](images/d9/d9c96e13ab078005333cdf02d8939c96d41fe6802b7f4caf0d4bab041cf8a314.png)"}]}
